---
description: Astro component conventions
globs: "**/*.astro"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Frontmatter (between `---`) runs at build time only. Never put secrets in client `<script>` tags; frontmatter is fine.
- Type props: `interface Props { title: string; tags?: string[] }` then `const { title, tags = [] } = Astro.props;`.
- Use `class:list={[...]}` for conditional classes and `set:html` only with trusted, sanitised HTML.
- Framework components need a `client:*` directive to be interactive; omit it when the component is static.
- Prefer `<Image />` from `astro:assets` over `<img>` for local images.
- Keep components small and composable; use `<slot />` (and named slots) instead of passing HTML strings as props.
- Scoped `<style>` by default; `:global()` only when styling slotted or third-party markup.
